	(text "USB2514 USB2 Hub"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 7.62 7.62)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7f4cd7aa-2a87-477a-9c2b-a0ec4e3f602f")
	)
	(text "Notes:\n\n1.	We choose the M2 version (SQFN package) since the QFN versions are labeled legacy and not reccomended (source: datasheet)\n2.	BC_EN pins can be left unconnected since they have internal pull downs. This disables battery charging feature for all ports\n3.	~{OCS} pins are active low with internal pull up. Since we are not controlling any power circuits, we can leave them disconnected\n4.	This hub is powered from the battery and is thus self-powered.\n5.	CFG_SEL pins are set to {00}. Configuration straps are used to configure the hub instead of SMBUS\n6.	We only need 2 ports. Hence, we disable ports 2 and 3 by pulling both pins up to 3.3V through a 10k resistor\n7.	NON_REM ports can be left pulled to ground since the removable-ness only needs to be indicated for certification tests of the hub as a consumer device. For our use case, it can be ignored\n8.	Power consumption on 3V3 rail (This estimate assumes all DFP are high speed devices)\n	-	Max: 85mA base + 25mA/ port * 2 = 145mA\n	-	Typical: 70mA base + 25mA/ port * 2 = 130mA\n9.	Crystal oscillator capacitance estimation\n	-	Load capacitance: 12pF\n	-	Estimated trace + pin capacitance: 3pF\n	-	C_1 = C_2 = 2 * (12 - 3) = 18pF\n10.	A maximum 3V3 rise time of 400us is allowed\n11.	References:\n	-	https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/aemDocuments/documents/OTH/ProductDocuments/BoardDesignFiles/EVB-USB2514B-FS_A1EvaluationBoardSchematicPDF.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.796 41.402 0)
		(effects
			(font
